# {{name}}

{{about}}

A [Pitwall](https://github.com/pitwalls/pitwall) tile, written in Rust with
`pitwall-extension` (preview: WIT `pitwall:tile@0.1.0`).

## Develop

```sh
rustup target add wasm32-wasip2   # once
pitwall extension dev             # build, check, load into Pitwall; again on every save
cargo test                        # the tests in tests/ run the built tile
pitwall extension check .         # the manifest, the component and its limits
```

`pitwall extension dev` builds with `cargo build --release --target
wasm32-wasip2`, copies the component to `tile.wasm` beside
`extension.json`, checks it, and asks the running Pitwall to load it as a
development extension (reloaded after each build, keeping its state).

## Files

| File | What |
|---|---|
| `extension.json` | The manifest: id, name, version, the tile (`contributes.tiles`), settings, permissions with your reasons |
| `src/lib.rs` | The tile: state, `render`, listeners |
| `tests/` | Tests with `pitwall-extension-test` |
